# config/instance.defaults — the skeleton's token list, with documentation.
#
# The repo contains NO operator-specific value: deployable files carry
# {{TOKENS}} and this file says what each one means. The values themselves live
# in data/instance.conf (untracked), written by the installer when it
# prompts, or by you by hand:
#
#   DOMAIN=example.com
#   HOSTNAME=server
#   ...
#
# scripts/render/render.sh substitutes them (`make render`, `make install-config`);
# compose files get the same names as ${DOMAIN} from the .env that
# `make render` writes next to each compose file.
#
# Keep this list alphabetical. Values here are EXAMPLES, never a real instance.

# DOMAIN — the public domain every vhost, cert and mail address uses (example.com)
# HOSTNAME — the machine name AND the tailnet node name (server)
# OPERATOR — the single login user on the box (root)
# GITHUB_USER — the GitHub account that owns the repos (exampleuser)
# REPO_NAME — the repository name (kefoCloud)
# REPO_DIR — absolute path of the checkout on the host (/root/github/kefoCloud)
# DATA_DIR — absolute path of all untracked instance state ($REPO_DIR/data)
# LOG_DIR — every log this project writes ($REPO_DIR/data/logs)
# SERVER_IP — the host's public IPv4 (needed for DNS + mail PTR checks)
# EMAIL — the operator's contact address (admin@$DOMAIN)
# TIMEZONE — IANA zone used by containers and cron (UTC)
#
# Prompted by the installer (with the domain):
# TAIL_ENDPOINT — "caddy" (LE cert for tail.$DOMAIN) or "tailscale" (tailscale
#                 serve publishes /ttyd under the machine's own HTTPS name).
#                 The installer never switches between them and takes no blank
#                 answer: every run must choose caddy or tailscale explicitly.
#
# Written by the installer:
# TS_CERT_HOST — the machine's own Tailscale HTTPS name (kefomachine.<tailnet>.ts.net)
# VIDEO_CALLING — "true" to run Talk (spreed + signaling + coturn); the talk
#                 vhost and its cert are rendered only when true.
# CLIENT_PUSH   — "true" to run notify_push and route cloud.$DOMAIN/push to it.
